# Rocci Blocks

**Audience:** experienced Rocci author.
**Prerequisites:** [standalone versus custom](/docs/concepts/standalone-versus-custom/).
**Role:** advanced standalone authoring example. Public copy says “falling-block arena.”

One shared SQLite game. Roc owns the board, the falling piece, gravity, kicks, and the seven-bag. Datastar `@post` / `@get` actions send intent. `@get:live("/sse")` morphs `#board` and `#hud`. There is no canvas island and no custom `main.roc`.

Run the backend entry so nested `backend/` and `ui/` modules resolve from this directory’s `rocci.toml`:

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- inspect --ast examples/rocci/standalone/blocks/backend/Blocks.rocci
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- inspect --ast examples/rocci/standalone/blocks/ui/BlocksUi.rocci
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/rocci/standalone/blocks/backend/Blocks.rocci
```

`--no-window` serves `http://127.0.0.1:8000/`. Open two tabs: a move in one morphs the board in both.

```sh
curl -s -o /dev/null -D - -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/actions/reset
# 204
curl -s -D - -o /dev/null -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/actions/reset \
  -H 'Datastar-Request: true'
# 200 text/event-stream (empty SSE)
```

Keyboard: arrows / WASD, Up/X rotate, Z CCW, Space hard drop.

## Layout

| Path | Owns |
| --- | --- |
| `backend/Blocks.rocci` | `@context`, `@init`, routes, SQLite |
| `backend/Game.roc` | Pure rules and overlay cells |
| `ui/BlocksUi.rocci` | Page, board, HUD, fixtures, CSS |

## Shortcomings

These are product limits of generated standalone Rocci, not accidental omissions:

- **Input latency.** Every key is an HTTP command. There is no client DAS/ARR; browser key-repeat posts instead.
- **Quoted keydown.** Rocci actions cannot branch on `evt.key`, so the keyboard map is opaque Datastar JS, not `@post("/actions/left")` on each key.
- **Gravity clock.** Generated live polls every 100 ms and applies due steps from `last_tick_ms`. Gravity does not advance with zero subscribers.
- **One shared game.** No cookies or seats. Every tab plays the same SQLite row.
- **HTML grid.** Cells remorph over SSE; this is not a 60 fps canvas paint.
- **No multiplayer protocol.** Garbage, spectators, leases, JSON lock acks, and a main-hostname play mount are out of this example. Snake remains the custom-runtime ceiling.
- **Generated `/health` only.** There is no extra health text route.
